-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 6 (Offences against the State, ss 121-130A),
-- Chapter 6A (Piracy, ss 130B-130C), Chapter 6B (Genocide, ss 130D-130E) and
-- Chapter 7 (Offences relating to the armed forces, ss 131-140B). Part of the
-- state-public group (Chapters 6-10).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt). Each section's text is quoted above its rules.
--
-- GENERATED by notes/state-public-gen/build.py from the hand-written ladders in
-- notes/state-public-gen/part_state.py; edit there and rebuild.
--
-- Many of these sections are abetment offences ("whoever abets ..."): "abets"
-- is s 107's word (pc-general-part), carried as a flat leaf and joined at
-- integration. ss 130A and 140A define "harbour" for their own Chapter only;
-- s 140B carries Chapter 7 over to the Singapore Police Force, and is encoded
-- as an OR beside every "officer or serviceman" leaf, cited.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-state-public-common`

§ `Chapter 6 - Offences against the State`

§§ `s 121 - Waging or attempting to wage war or abetting the waging of war against the Government`

--   121. Whoever wages war against the Government, or attempts to wage such war,
--   or abets the waging of such war, shall be punished with death, or with
--   imprisonment for life.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   A joins an insurrection against the Government. A has committed the offence
--   defined in this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121
DECLARE `Waging War Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `wages war against the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused wage war against the Government? Joining an insurrection against the Government is waging war (s 121 illustration).
    `attempts to wage such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to wage such war?
    `abets the waging of such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused abet the waging of such war (s 107 - pc-general-part; joined at integration)?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121
`punishment prescribed by s 121` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "121"
    words                    IS "death, or with imprisonment for life"
    death                    IS `or with`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- Not named `wages war against the Government`: that is the first leaf's name, and a
-- rule named like a field of its own input silently calls ITSELF where the ladder reads
-- the field - measured: `assertion could not be evaluated: Stack overflow`, no other
-- diagnostic. notes/state-public-forks.md SP-0.
@export Whether the accused wages, attempts to wage, or abets the waging of war against the Government, within section 121 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Waging War Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wages, attempts or abets war against the Government` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `wages war against the Government`
         OR  f's `attempts to wage such war`
         OR  f's `abets the waging of such war` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 121 of the Penal Code 1871 (waging war against the Government)
GIVEN f IS A `Waging War Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 121` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wages, attempts or abets war against the Government` f

@export Frame a charge under section 121 of the Penal Code 1871 (waging or attempting to wage war or abetting the waging of war against the Government), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Waging War Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 121` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "121" "waging or attempting to wage war or abetting the waging of war against the Government"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 121`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 121` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `wages war against the Government`) "wage war"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to wage such war`) "attempt to wage war"), (`included if` (f's `abets the waging of such war`) "abet the waging of war"))), " against the Government", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `wages war against the Government` OR f's `attempts to wage such war` OR f's `abets the waging of such war`) "wages war against the Government, or attempts to wage, or abets the waging of, such war")))

§§ `s 121A - Offences against the President's person`

--   121A. Whoever plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or
--   restraint of the President, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or
--   for a term which may extend to 20 years and shall, if he is not sentenced to
--   imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 121A, 121B, 121C
DECLARE `Plot against the President Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 121A: Did the accused plan the death of, hurt to, or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President?
    `plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 121B: Did the accused plan the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore?
    `plans the overawing by criminal force of the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 121B: Did the accused plan the overawing of the Government by criminal force (s 350)?
    `abets the commission of any of the offences punishable by section 121A or 121B`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 121C: Did the accused abet (s 107) the commission of an offence punishable by s 121A or 121B?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121A
`punishment prescribed by s 121A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "121A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or for a term which may extend to 20 years and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- ss 121A-121D each define and punish in one clause with a single element group;
-- the offence ladder is the defining predicate.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 121A of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against the President's person)
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 121A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President`

@export Frame a charge under section 121A of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against the President's person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 121A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "121A" "offences against the President's person"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 121A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 121A` f)
        (CONCAT "did plan the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President`) "plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President")))

§§ `s 121B - Offences against authority`

--   121B. Whoever plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President
--   from the sovereignty of Singapore, or the overawing by criminal force of the
--   Government, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or for a term which
--   may extend to 20 years and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for
--   life, also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121B
`punishment prescribed by s 121B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "121B"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or for a term which may extend to 20 years and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 121B of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against authority)
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 121B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore`
         OR  f's `plans the overawing by criminal force of the Government` )

@export Frame a charge under section 121B of the Penal Code 1871 (offences against authority), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 121B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "121B" "offences against authority"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 121B`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 121B` f)
        (CONCAT "did plan ", (IF f's `plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore` THEN "the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore" ELSE "the overawing by criminal force of the Government"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore` OR f's `plans the overawing by criminal force of the Government`) "plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President, or the overawing by criminal force of the Government")))

§§ `s 121C - Abetting offences under section 121A or 121B`

--   121C. Whoever abets the commission of any of the offences punishable by
--   section 121A or 121B shall be punished with the punishment provided for
--   those offences.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121C
`punishment prescribed by s 121C` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "121C"
    words                    IS "the punishment provided for those offences - under sections 121A and 121B, imprisonment for life or for a term which may extend to 20 years and, if not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- FORK SP-121C: the punishment is "the punishment provided for those offences",
-- which ss 121A and 121B state identically; recorded as theirs.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 121C of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting an offence under section 121A or 121B)
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 121C` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `abets the commission of any of the offences punishable by section 121A or 121B`

@export Frame a charge under section 121C of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting an offence under section 121A or 121B), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Plot against the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 121C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "121C" "abetting an offence under section 121A or 121B"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 121C`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 121C` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet the commission of an offence punishable by section 121A or 121B of the Penal Code 1871", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the commission of any of the offences punishable by section 121A or 121B`) "abets the commission of an offence punishable by section 121A or 121B")))

§§ `s 121D - Intentional omission to give information of offences against section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C by a person bound to inform`

--   121D. Whoever knowing or having reason to believe that any offence
--   punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed
--   intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence which he
--   is legally bound to give, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121D
DECLARE `Omission to Inform of Offence against the State Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `knowing that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know that an offence punishable under s 121, 121A, 121B or 121C had been committed?
    `having reason to believe that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have reason to believe (s 26) that such an offence had been committed?
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `omits to give any information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused fail to give information about that offence which the accused was legally bound (s 43) to give?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 121D
`punishment prescribed by s 121D` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "121D"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 121D of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to give information of an offence against the State)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform of Offence against the State Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 121D` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `knowing that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed`
         OR  f's `having reason to believe that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed` )
    AND f's intentionally
    AND f's `omits to give any information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give`

@export Frame a charge under section 121D of the Penal Code 1871 (intentional omission to give information of an offence against the State), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform of Offence against the State Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 121D` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "121D" "intentional omission to give information of an offence against the State"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 121D`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 121D` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `knowing that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed` THEN "knowing" ELSE "having reason to believe"), " that an offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C of the Penal Code 1871 had been committed, did intentionally omit to give information respecting that offence which you were legally bound to give", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed` OR f's `having reason to believe that any offence punishable under section 121, 121A, 121B or 121C has been committed`) "knowing or having reason to believe that such an offence has been committed"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to give any information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give`) "omits to give information he is legally bound to give")))

§§ `s 122 - Collecting arms, etc., with the intention of waging war against the Government`

--   122. Whoever collects men, arms or ammunition or otherwise prepares to wage
--   war, with the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war
--   against the Government, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or
--   imprisonment for a term not exceeding 20 years, and shall, if he is not
--   sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 122
DECLARE `Preparing War Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `collects men, arms or ammunition`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused collect men, arms or ammunition?
    `otherwise prepares to wage war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused otherwise prepare to wage war?
    `with the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to wage, or to be prepared to wage, war against the Government?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 122
`punishment prescribed by s 122` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "122"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 122 of the Penal Code 1871 (collecting arms with the intention of waging war against the Government)
GIVEN f IS A `Preparing War Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 122` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `collects men, arms or ammunition`
         OR  f's `otherwise prepares to wage war` )
    AND f's `with the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government`

@export Frame a charge under section 122 of the Penal Code 1871 (collecting arms with the intention of waging war against the Government), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Preparing War Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 122` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "122" "collecting arms with the intention of waging war against the Government"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 122`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 122` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `collects men, arms or ammunition` THEN "collect men, arms or ammunition" ELSE "prepare to wage war"), ", with the intention of waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `collects men, arms or ammunition` OR f's `otherwise prepares to wage war`) "collects men, arms or ammunition, or otherwise prepares to wage war"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government`) "with the intention of waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government")))

§§ `s 123 - Concealing with intent to facilitate a design to wage war`

--   123. Whoever by any act, or by any illegal omission, conceals the existence
--   of a design to wage war against the Government, intending by such
--   concealment to facilitate, or knowing it to be likely that such concealment
--   will facilitate, the waging of such war, shall be punished with imprisonment
--   for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 123
DECLARE `Concealing Design to Wage War Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `by any act`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the concealment by an act?
    `by any illegal omission`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the concealment by an illegal (s 43) omission?
    `conceals the existence of a design to wage war against the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused conceal the existence of a design to wage war against the Government?
    `intending by such concealment to facilitate the waging of such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the concealment to facilitate the waging of that war?
    `knowing it to be likely that such concealment will facilitate the waging of such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it likely the concealment would facilitate it?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 123
`punishment prescribed by s 123` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "123"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 123 of the Penal Code 1871 (concealing a design to wage war)
GIVEN f IS A `Concealing Design to Wage War Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 123` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `by any act`
         OR  f's `by any illegal omission` )
    AND f's `conceals the existence of a design to wage war against the Government`
    AND (    f's `intending by such concealment to facilitate the waging of such war`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that such concealment will facilitate the waging of such war` )

@export Frame a charge under section 123 of the Penal Code 1871 (concealing with intent to facilitate a design to wage war), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Concealing Design to Wage War Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 123` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "123" "concealing with intent to facilitate a design to wage war"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 123`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 123` f)
        (CONCAT "did conceal the existence of a design to wage war against the Government, ", (IF f's `intending by such concealment to facilitate the waging of such war` THEN "intending" ELSE "knowing it to be likely"), " by such concealment to facilitate the waging of such war", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `by any act` OR f's `by any illegal omission`) "by an act or an illegal omission"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `conceals the existence of a design to wage war against the Government`) "conceals the existence of a design to wage war against the Government"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending by such concealment to facilitate the waging of such war` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that such concealment will facilitate the waging of such war`) "intending, or knowing it likely, that the concealment will facilitate the war")))

§§ `s 124 - Assaulting President, etc., with intent to compel or restrain the exercise of any lawful power`

--   124. Whoever, with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or
--   a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, to exercise or refrain from
--   exercising in any manner any of the lawful powers of the President, or such
--   Member, assaults or wrongfully restrains, or attempts wrongfully to
--   restrain, or overawes by means of criminal force, or the show of criminal
--   force, or attempts so to overawe, the President or such Member, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for life or for a term which may extend to 20
--   years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be
--   liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 124
DECLARE `Assaulting the President Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising in any manner any of their lawful powers`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to induce or compel the President, a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise, or refrain from exercising, any of their lawful powers?
    assaults
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused assault the President or such Member (s 351 - pc-body-a; joined at integration)?
    `wrongfully restrains`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused wrongfully restrain them (s 339 - pc-body-a; joined at integration)?
    `attempts wrongfully to restrain`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt wrongfully to restrain them?
    `overawes by means of criminal force, or the show of criminal force`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused overawe them by criminal force or the show of criminal force?
    `attempts so to overawe`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt so to overawe them?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 124
`punishment prescribed by s 124` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "124"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 124 of the Penal Code 1871 (assaulting the President, etc., with intent to compel or restrain the exercise of lawful power)
GIVEN f IS AN `Assaulting the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 124` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    AND f's `with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising in any manner any of their lawful powers`
    AND (    f's assaults
         OR  f's `wrongfully restrains`
         OR  f's `attempts wrongfully to restrain`
         OR  f's `overawes by means of criminal force, or the show of criminal force`
         OR  f's `attempts so to overawe` )
    AND "the President or such Member"

@export Frame a charge under section 124 of the Penal Code 1871 (assaulting the President or a Member of Parliament with intent to compel or restrain the exercise of lawful power), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Assaulting the President Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 124` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "124" "assaulting the President or a Member of Parliament with intent to compel or restrain the exercise of lawful power"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 124`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 124` f)
        (CONCAT "with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising a lawful power, did ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's assaults) "assault"), (`included if` (f's `wrongfully restrains`) "wrongfully restrain"), (`included if` (f's `attempts wrongfully to restrain`) "attempt wrongfully to restrain"), (`included if` (f's `overawes by means of criminal force, or the show of criminal force`) "overawe by means of criminal force"), (`included if` (f's `attempts so to overawe`) "attempt so to overawe"))), " the President or such Member", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising in any manner any of their lawful powers`) "with the intention of inducing or compelling the exercise or non-exercise of a lawful power"),
            (`missing unless` (f's assaults OR f's `wrongfully restrains` OR f's `attempts wrongfully to restrain` OR f's `overawes by means of criminal force, or the show of criminal force` OR f's `attempts so to overawe`) "assaults, wrongfully restrains or attempts to, or overawes by criminal force or attempts to")))

§§ `s 125 - Waging war against any power in alliance or at peace with Singapore`

--   125. Whoever wages war against the government of any power in alliance or at
--   peace with the Government, or attempts to wage such war, or abets the waging
--   of such war, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, to which fine may be
--   added, or with fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 125, 126, 127
DECLARE `War against an Allied Power Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `wages war against the government of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 125: Did the accused wage war against the government of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government?
    `attempts to wage such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 125: Did the accused attempt to wage such war?
    `abets the waging of such war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 125: Did the accused abet (s 107) the waging of such war?
    `commits depredation`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 126: Did the accused commit depredation (plunder)?
    `makes preparations to commit depredation`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 126: Did the accused make preparations to commit depredation?
    `on the territories of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 126: ... on the territories of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government?
    `receives any property`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 127: Did the accused receive property?
    `knowing the same to have been taken in the commission of any of the offences mentioned in sections 125 and 126`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 127: Did the accused know it had been taken in committing an offence mentioned in s 125 or 126?
    `the property`
        IS A STRING @desc s 127: The property received, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 125
`punishment prescribed by s 125` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "125"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, to which fine may be added, or with fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- FORK SP-125: "imprisonment ... to which fine may be added, or with fine" - fine is recorded
-- `or with` (it may stand alone); that it may also be ADDED to a term is in the words only.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 125 of the Penal Code 1871 (waging war against a power in alliance or at peace with Singapore)
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 125` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `wages war against the government of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`
         OR  f's `attempts to wage such war`
         OR  f's `abets the waging of such war` )

@export Frame a charge under section 125 of the Penal Code 1871 (waging war against a power in alliance or at peace with Singapore), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 125` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "125" "waging war against a power in alliance or at peace with Singapore"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 125`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 125` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `wages war against the government of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`) "wage war"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to wage such war`) "attempt to wage war"), (`included if` (f's `abets the waging of such war`) "abet the waging of war"))), " against the government of a power at peace with the Government", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `wages war against the government of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government` OR f's `attempts to wage such war` OR f's `abets the waging of such war`) "wages, attempts to wage, or abets the waging of war against a power in alliance or at peace with the Government")))

§§ `s 126 - Committing depredation on the territories of any power in alliance or at peace with Singapore`

--   126. Whoever commits depredation, or makes preparations to commit
--   depredation, on the territories of any power in alliance or at peace with
--   the Government, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine, and any property used,
--   or intended to be used, in committing such depredation, or acquired by such
--   depredation, shall be forfeited.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 126
`punishment prescribed by s 126` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "126"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine, and any property used, or intended to be used, in committing such depredation, or acquired by such depredation, shall be forfeited"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `shall be punished with`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 126 of the Penal Code 1871 (committing depredation on the territories of a power at peace with Singapore)
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 126` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `commits depredation`
         OR  f's `makes preparations to commit depredation` )
    AND f's `on the territories of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`

@export Frame a charge under section 126 of the Penal Code 1871 (committing depredation on the territories of a power at peace with Singapore), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 126` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "126" "committing depredation on the territories of a power at peace with Singapore"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 126`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 126` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `commits depredation` THEN "commit depredation" ELSE "make preparations to commit depredation"), " on the territories of a power at peace with the Government", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `commits depredation` OR f's `makes preparations to commit depredation`) "commits, or prepares to commit, depredation"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `on the territories of any power in alliance or at peace with the Government`) "on the territories of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government")))

§§ `s 127 - Receiving property taken by war or depredation mentioned in sections 125 and 126`

--   127. Whoever receives any property knowing the same to have been taken in
--   the commission of any of the offences mentioned in sections 125 and 126,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years,
--   and shall also be liable to fine, and the property so received shall be
--   forfeited.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 127
`punishment prescribed by s 127` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "127"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine, and the property so received shall be forfeited"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `shall be punished with`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 127 of the Penal Code 1871 (receiving property taken by war or depredation)
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 127` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `receives any property`
    AND f's `knowing the same to have been taken in the commission of any of the offences mentioned in sections 125 and 126`

@export Frame a charge under section 127 of the Penal Code 1871 (receiving property taken by war or depredation), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `War against an Allied Power Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 127` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "127" "receiving property taken by war or depredation"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 127`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 127` f)
        (CONCAT "did receive ", f's `the property`, ", knowing the same to have been taken in the commission of an offence mentioned in section 125 or 126 of the Penal Code 1871", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `receives any property`) "receives any property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing the same to have been taken in the commission of any of the offences mentioned in sections 125 and 126`) "knowing it to have been taken in committing an offence under section 125 or 126")))

§§ `s 128 - Public servant voluntarily allowing prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape`

--   128. Whoever, being a public servant, and having the custody of any prisoner
--   of State or prisoner of war, voluntarily allows such prisoner to escape from
--   any place in which such prisoner is confined, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15
--   years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be
--   liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 128, 129
DECLARE `Prisoner of State Custody Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `having the custody of any prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war?
    voluntarily
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 128: Did the accused allow the escape voluntarily (s 26A)?
    negligently
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 129: Did the accused suffer the escape negligently (s 26F)?
    `such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the prisoner escape from the place of confinement? (s 130 Explanation: a prisoner at large on parole within limits escapes by going beyond them.)
    `the prisoner`
        IS A Person @desc The prisoner, as the charge names them
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 128
`punishment prescribed by s 128` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "128"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 128 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape)
GIVEN f IS A `Prisoner of State Custody Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 128` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `having the custody of any prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
    AND f's voluntarily
    AND "allows"
    AND f's `such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined`

@export Frame a charge under section 128 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Prisoner of State Custody Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 128` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "128" "public servant voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 128`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 128` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant having the custody of ", `one person` (f's `the prisoner`), ", a prisoner of State or prisoner of war, did voluntarily allow the said prisoner to escape from the place in which ", `subject pronoun` (f's `the prisoner`'s pronoun), " was confined", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `having the custody of any prisoner of State or prisoner of war`) "having the custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war"),
            (`missing unless` (f's voluntarily) "voluntarily"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined`) "such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined")))

§§ `s 129 - Public servant negligently suffering prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape`

--   129. Whoever, being a public servant, and having the custody of any prisoner
--   of State or prisoner of war, negligently suffers such prisoner to escape
--   from any place of confinement in which such prisoner is confined, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall
--   also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 129
`punishment prescribed by s 129` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "129"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 129 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape)
GIVEN f IS A `Prisoner of State Custody Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 129` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `having the custody of any prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
    AND f's negligently
    AND "suffers"
    AND f's `such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined`

@export Frame a charge under section 129 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Prisoner of State Custody Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 129` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "129" "public servant negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war in his custody to escape"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 129`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 129` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant having the custody of ", `one person` (f's `the prisoner`), ", a prisoner of State or prisoner of war, did negligently suffer the said prisoner to escape from the place of confinement in which ", `subject pronoun` (f's `the prisoner`'s pronoun), " was confined", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `having the custody of any prisoner of State or prisoner of war`) "having the custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war"),
            (`missing unless` (f's negligently) "negligently"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined`) "such prisoner escapes from the place in which he is confined")))

§§ `s 130 - Aiding escape of, rescuing, or harbouring such prisoner`

--   130. Whoever knowingly aids or assists any prisoner of State or prisoner of
--   war in escaping from lawful custody or rescues or attempts to rescue any
--   such prisoner, or harbours or conceals any such prisoner who has escaped
--   from lawful custody, or offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the
--   recapture of such prisoner, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or
--   with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall, if he
--   is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.
--
--   Explanation.-A prisoner of State or prisoner of war who is permitted to be
--   at large on his parole within certain limits in Singapore, is said to escape
--   from lawful custody if he goes beyond the limits within which he is allowed
--   to be at large.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130 and its Explanation; s 130A
DECLARE `Aiding Escape of Prisoner of State Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    knowingly
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act knowingly (s 26D)? Read as governing every limb (FORK SP-130).
    `aids or assists any prisoner of State or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused aid or assist a prisoner of State or of war in escaping from lawful custody? (Explanation: a prisoner at large on parole within limits in Singapore escapes by going beyond them.)
    `rescues or attempts to rescue any such prisoner`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused rescue, or attempt to rescue, such a prisoner?
    `harbours or conceals any such prisoner who has escaped from lawful custody`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused harbour (s 130A: including supplying shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition or conveyance, or helping to evade apprehension) or conceal such a prisoner who had escaped?
    `offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the recapture of such prisoner`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused offer, or attempt to offer, resistance to the prisoner's recapture?
    `the prisoner`
        IS A Person @desc The prisoner, as the charge names them
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130
`punishment prescribed by s 130` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 130 of the Penal Code 1871 (aiding the escape of, rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war)
GIVEN f IS AN `Aiding Escape of Prisoner of State Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 130` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's knowingly
    AND (    f's `aids or assists any prisoner of State or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody`
         OR  f's `rescues or attempts to rescue any such prisoner`
         OR  f's `harbours or conceals any such prisoner who has escaped from lawful custody`
         OR  f's `offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the recapture of such prisoner` )

@export Frame a charge under section 130 of the Penal Code 1871 (aiding the escape of, rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Aiding Escape of Prisoner of State Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 130` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "130" "aiding the escape of, rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 130`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 130` f)
        (CONCAT "did knowingly ", `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `aids or assists any prisoner of State or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody`) "aid"), (`included if` (f's `rescues or attempts to rescue any such prisoner`) "rescue or attempt to rescue"), (`included if` (f's `harbours or conceals any such prisoner who has escaped from lawful custody`) "harbour"), (`included if` (f's `offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the recapture of such prisoner`) "offer resistance to the recapture of"))), " ", `one person` (f's `the prisoner`), ", a prisoner of State or prisoner of war", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's knowingly) "knowingly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `aids or assists any prisoner of State or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody` OR f's `rescues or attempts to rescue any such prisoner` OR f's `harbours or conceals any such prisoner who has escaped from lawful custody` OR f's `offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the recapture of such prisoner`) "aids the escape of, rescues, harbours or conceals, or resists the recapture of, such a prisoner")))

§§ `s 130A - "Harbour"`

--   130A. In this Chapter, "harbour" includes the supplying a person with
--   shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of
--   conveyance, or the assisting a person in any way to evade apprehension.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 130A, 140A
DECLARE `Harbour Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `harbours the person in the ordinary sense of the word`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused harbour the person in the ordinary sense - give them refuge? ("harbour" INCLUDES the limbs below; it is not confined to them.)
    `supplies the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused supply the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition or means of conveyance?
    `assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused assist the person in any way to evade apprehension?

-- "includes" widens the word, so the ordinary meaning is kept as a first limb.
-- No charge: a definition. It is the drill-down for the harbouring leaf of s 130.
@export Whether the accused "harbours" a person, as Chapter 6 of the Penal Code 1871 uses the word (s 130A)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbour Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours within section 130A` f IF
        "In this Chapter, 'harbour' includes"
    ..  f's `harbours the person in the ordinary sense of the word`
    OR  f's `supplies the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance`
    OR  f's `assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`

§ `Chapter 6A - Piracy`

§§ `s 130B - Piracy by law of nations`

--   130B.-(1) A person commits piracy who does any act that, by the law of
--   nations, is piracy.
--
--   (2) Whoever commits piracy shall be punished with imprisonment for life and
--   shall be liable to caning, but if while committing or attempting to commit
--   piracy he murders or attempts to murder another person or does any act that
--   is likely to endanger the life of another person he shall be punished with
--   death.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130B
DECLARE `Piracy Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `does any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do an act that is piracy by the law of nations? (A question of international law - for example art 101 of the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea - which is not in this job's inputs; the answer is the investigator's to supply.)
    `while committing or attempting to commit piracy, murders or attempts to murder another person or does any act that is likely to endanger the life of another person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc While committing or attempting to commit piracy, did the accused murder or attempt to murder another person, or do an act likely to endanger another person's life? This chooses the punishment (death); murder is s 300 - pc-body-a.
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130B(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 130B(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130B(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life and shall be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `shall be punished with`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130B(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 130B(2), where the pirate murders or endangers life` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130B(2)"
    words                    IS "death"
    death                    IS `shall be punished with`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused "commits piracy" within section 130B(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Piracy Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits piracy` f IF
        "(1) A person commits piracy who"
    ... f's `does any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 130B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (piracy)
GIVEN f IS A `Piracy Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 130B(2)` f IF
        "(2) Whoever"
    ... `commits piracy` f

@export Frame a charge under section 130B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (piracy by the law of nations), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Piracy Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 130B(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "130B(2)" "piracy by the law of nations"
        (IF f's `while committing or attempting to commit piracy, murders or attempts to murder another person or does any act that is likely to endanger the life of another person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 130B(2), where the pirate murders or endangers life`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 130B(2)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 130B(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did commit piracy, being an act that by the law of nations is piracy", (IF f's `while committing or attempting to commit piracy, murders or attempts to murder another person or does any act that is likely to endanger the life of another person` THEN ", and while committing such piracy did an act likely to endanger the life of another person" ELSE ""), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `does any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy`) "does an act that, by the law of nations, is piracy")))

§§ `s 130C - Piratical acts`

--   130C. Whoever, while in or out of Singapore - (a) steals a Singapore ship;
--   (b) steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys
--   anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore
--   ship; (c) does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship; or (d)
--   counsels or procures a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b)
--   or (c), shall be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15
--   years and shall be liable to caning.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130C
DECLARE `Piratical Acts Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `steals a Singapore ship`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused steal a Singapore ship (theft, s 378 - pc-property; joined at integration)?
    `steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused steal, or without lawful authority throw overboard, damage or destroy, any of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship?
    `does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused do, or attempt to do, a mutinous act on a Singapore ship?
    `counsels or procures a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Did the accused counsel or procure anyone to do any of those things?
    `the ship`
        IS A STRING @desc The Singapore ship, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130C
`punishment prescribed by s 130C` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130C"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15 years and shall be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 130C of the Penal Code 1871 (piratical acts)
GIVEN f IS A `Piratical Acts Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 130C` f IF
        "Whoever, while in or out of Singapore -"
    ..  f's `steals a Singapore ship`
    OR  f's `steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship`
    OR  f's `does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship`
    OR  f's `counsels or procures a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`

@export Frame a charge under section 130C of the Penal Code 1871 (piratical acts), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Piratical Acts Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 130C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "130C" "piratical acts"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 130C`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 130C` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `steals a Singapore ship`) "steal"), (`included if` (f's `steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship`) "without lawful authority damage the cargo, supplies or fittings in"), (`included if` (f's `does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship`) "do a mutinous act on"), (`included if` (f's `counsels or procures a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`) "counsel or procure a piratical act on"))), " ", f's `the ship`, ", a Singapore ship", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `steals a Singapore ship` OR f's `steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship` OR f's `does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship` OR f's `counsels or procures a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`) "one of the acts in section 130C(a) to (d)")))

§ `Chapter 6B - Genocide`

§§ `s 130D - Genocide`

--   130D. A person commits genocide who, with intent to destroy, in whole or in
--   part, a national, an ethnical, a racial or a religious group, commits any of
--   the following acts: (a) killing members of the group; (b) causing serious
--   bodily or mental harm to members of the group; (c) deliberately inflicting
--   on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical
--   destruction in whole or in part; (d) imposing measures intended to prevent
--   births within the group; or (e) forcibly transferring children of the group
--   to another group.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 130D, 130E
DECLARE `Genocide Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, an ethnical, a racial or a religious group`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group?
    `killing members of the group`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) killing members of the group?
    `causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group?
    `deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part?
    `imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group?
    `forcibly transferring children of the group to another group`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) forcibly transferring children of the group to another group?
    `the offence consists of the killing of any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 130E(a): Does the offence consist of the killing of any person? This chooses the punishment (death); it is not an element.
    `the group`
        IS A STRING @desc The group, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@export Whether the accused "commits genocide" within section 130D of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Genocide Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits genocide` f IF
        "A person commits genocide who,"
    AND f's `with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, an ethnical, a racial or a religious group`
    AND "commits any of the following acts:"
    AND (    f's `killing members of the group`
         OR  f's `causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group`
         OR  f's `deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part`
         OR  f's `imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group`
         OR  f's `forcibly transferring children of the group to another group` )

§§ `s 130E - Punishment for genocide`

--   130E. Whoever commits genocide shall - (a) if the offence consists of the
--   killing of any person, be punished with death; or (b) in any other case, be
--   punished with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment for a term which
--   may extend to 20 years.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130E(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 130E(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130E(a)"
    words                    IS "death"
    death                    IS `shall be punished with`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 130E(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 130E(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "130E(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 130E of the Penal Code 1871 (genocide)
GIVEN f IS A `Genocide Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 130E` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `commits genocide` f

@export Frame a charge under section 130E of the Penal Code 1871 (genocide), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Genocide Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 130E` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the offence consists of the killing of any person` THEN "130E(a)" ELSE "130E(b)") "genocide"
        (IF f's `the offence consists of the killing of any person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 130E(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 130E(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 130E` f)
        (CONCAT "with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, ", f's `the group`, ", did commit genocide", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, an ethnical, a racial or a religious group`) "with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `killing members of the group` OR f's `causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group` OR f's `deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part` OR f's `imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group` OR f's `forcibly transferring children of the group to another group`) "one of the acts in section 130D(a) to (e)"),
            (`missing unless` (`commits genocide` f) "the elements of section 130D taken together")))

§ `Chapter 7 - Offences relating to the armed forces`

§§ `s 131 - Abetting mutiny, or attempting to seduce an officer or a serviceman from his duty`

--   131. Whoever abets the committing of mutiny by an officer or any serviceman
--   in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in
--   Singapore or attempts to seduce any such officer or serviceman from his
--   allegiance or his duty, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or
--   with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he
--   is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 131-138, 140B
DECLARE `Armed Forces Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is (or was) the person concerned an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces, or in any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore?
    `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 140B: Is (or was) the person concerned a member of the Singapore Police Force, or of a volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to or under its jurisdiction? Chapter 7 applies to them "with the necessary modifications".
    `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 131, 132: Did the accused abet (s 107) the committing of mutiny by such an officer or serviceman?
    `attempts to seduce such officer or serviceman from his allegiance or his duty`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 131: Did the accused attempt to seduce such an officer or serviceman from allegiance or duty?
    `mutiny is committed in consequence of that abetment`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 132: Was mutiny committed in consequence of the abetment?
    `abets an assault by such officer or serviceman on any superior officer being in the execution of his office`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 133, 134: Did the accused abet an assault by such an officer or serviceman on a superior officer in the execution of office?
    `such assault is committed in consequence of that abetment`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 134: Was the assault committed in consequence of the abetment?
    `abets the desertion of such officer or serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 135: Did the accused abet the desertion of such an officer or serviceman?
    `knowing or having reason to believe that such officer or serviceman has deserted`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 136: Did the accused know or have reason to believe (s 26) that such an officer or serviceman had deserted?
    `harbours such officer or serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 136: Did the accused harbour them (s 140A: including supplying shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition or conveyance, or helping to evade apprehension)?
    `with the intention of preventing the officer or serviceman from being apprehended`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 136: ... intending to prevent their apprehension?
    `abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by such officer or serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 138: Did the accused abet what the accused knew to be an act of insubordination by such an officer or serviceman?
    `such act of insubordination is committed in consequence of that abetment`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 138: Was the act of insubordination committed in consequence of the abetment?
    `the serviceman`
        IS A Person @desc The officer or serviceman, as the charge names them
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 131
`punishment prescribed by s 131` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "131"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 131 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting mutiny, or attempting to seduce an officer or serviceman from duty)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 131` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman`
         OR  f's `attempts to seduce such officer or serviceman from his allegiance or his duty` )
    AND "the person concerned being"
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )

@export Frame a charge under section 131 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetting mutiny, or attempting to seduce an officer or a serviceman from his duty), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 131` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "131" "abetting mutiny, or attempting to seduce an officer or a serviceman from his duty"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 131`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 131` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman` THEN "abet the committing of mutiny by " ELSE "attempt to seduce from his allegiance or his duty "), `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman` OR f's `attempts to seduce such officer or serviceman from his allegiance or his duty`) "abets mutiny by, or attempts to seduce from allegiance or duty"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)")))

§§ `s 132 - Abetment of mutiny, if mutiny is committed in consequence thereof`

--   132. Whoever abets the committing of mutiny by an officer or any serviceman
--   in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in
--   Singapore shall, if mutiny be committed in consequence of that abetment, be
--   punished with death or with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for
--   a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to
--   death or imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 132
`punishment prescribed by s 132` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "132"
    words                    IS "death or with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to death or imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `or with`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 132 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of mutiny, if mutiny is committed in consequence)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 132` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman`
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )
    AND "shall, if"
    AND f's `mutiny is committed in consequence of that abetment`

@export Frame a charge under section 132 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of mutiny, mutiny being committed in consequence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 132` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "132" "abetment of mutiny, mutiny being committed in consequence"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 132`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 132` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet the committing of mutiny by ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), ", and mutiny was committed in consequence of that abetment", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the committing of mutiny by such officer or serviceman`) "abets the committing of mutiny"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "by an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `mutiny is committed in consequence of that abetment`) "mutiny is committed in consequence of that abetment")))

§§ `s 133 - Abetment of an assault by an officer or a serviceman on his superior officer, when in the execution of his office`

--   133. Whoever abets an assault by an officer or any serviceman in the
--   Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore,
--   on any superior officer being in the execution of his office, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall
--   also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 133
`punishment prescribed by s 133` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "133"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 133 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an assault by an officer or serviceman on a superior officer)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 133` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `abets an assault by such officer or serviceman on any superior officer being in the execution of his office`
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )

@export Frame a charge under section 133 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an assault by an officer or a serviceman on a superior officer), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 133` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "133" "abetment of an assault by an officer or a serviceman on a superior officer"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 133`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 133` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet an assault by ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), " on a superior officer being in the execution of his office", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets an assault by such officer or serviceman on any superior officer being in the execution of his office`) "abets an assault on a superior officer in the execution of his office"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "by an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)")))

§§ `s 134 - Abetment of such assault, if the assault is committed`

--   134. Whoever abets an assault by an officer or any serviceman in the
--   Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore,
--   on any superior officer being in the execution of his office, shall, if such
--   assault be committed in consequence of that abetment, be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
--   liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 134
`punishment prescribed by s 134` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "134"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 134 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an assault on a superior officer, the assault being committed)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 134` f IF
        `offence under s 133` f
    AND "shall, if"
    AND f's `such assault is committed in consequence of that abetment`

@export Frame a charge under section 134 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an assault by an officer or a serviceman on a superior officer, the assault being committed), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 134` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "134" "abetment of an assault by an officer or a serviceman on a superior officer, the assault being committed"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 134`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 134` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet an assault by ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), " on a superior officer being in the execution of his office, and such assault was committed in consequence of that abetment", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets an assault by such officer or serviceman on any superior officer being in the execution of his office`) "abets an assault on a superior officer in the execution of his office"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "by an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `such assault is committed in consequence of that abetment`) "such assault is committed in consequence of that abetment")))

§§ `s 135 - Abetment of the desertion of an officer or a serviceman`

--   135. Whoever abets the desertion of any officer or any serviceman in the
--   Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years,
--   or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 135
`punishment prescribed by s 135` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "135"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 135 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of the desertion of an officer or serviceman)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 135` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `abets the desertion of such officer or serviceman`
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )

@export Frame a charge under section 135 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of the desertion of an officer or a serviceman), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 135` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "135" "abetment of the desertion of an officer or a serviceman"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 135`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 135` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet the desertion of ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the desertion of such officer or serviceman`) "abets the desertion"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "of an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)")))

§§ `s 136 - Harbouring a deserter`

--   136. Whoever knowing or having reason to believe that an officer or a
--   serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully
--   present in Singapore has deserted, harbours such officer or serviceman with
--   the intention of preventing the officer or serviceman from being
--   apprehended, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--   to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 136
`punishment prescribed by s 136` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "136"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 136 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring a deserter)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 136` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowing or having reason to believe that such officer or serviceman has deserted`
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )
    AND f's `harbours such officer or serviceman`
    AND f's `with the intention of preventing the officer or serviceman from being apprehended`

@export Frame a charge under section 136 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring a deserter), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 136` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "136" "harbouring a deserter"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 136`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 136` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), " had deserted, did harbour ", `object pronoun` (f's `the serviceman`'s pronoun), " with the intention of preventing ", `object pronoun` (f's `the serviceman`'s pronoun), " from being apprehended", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that such officer or serviceman has deserted`) "knowing or having reason to believe that he has deserted"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `harbours such officer or serviceman`) "harbours such officer or serviceman"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of preventing the officer or serviceman from being apprehended`) "with the intention of preventing his apprehension")))

§§ `s 137 - Deserter concealed on board merchant vessel through negligence of master`

--   137. The master or person in charge of a merchant vessel, on board of which
--   any deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully
--   present in Singapore is concealed, shall, though ignorant of such
--   concealment, be punished with a fine not exceeding $1,500, if he might have
--   known of such concealment, but for some neglect of his duty as such master
--   or person in charge, or but for some want of discipline on board of the
--   vessel.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 137; s 140B
DECLARE `Deserter on Merchant Vessel Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel?
    `on board of which any deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore is concealed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by s 140B, the Singapore Police Force) concealed on board?
    `he might have known of such concealment, but for some neglect of his duty as such master or person in charge, or but for some want of discipline on board of the vessel`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might the accused have known of the concealment but for some neglect of duty, or some want of discipline on board? ("though ignorant of such concealment" - actual ignorance is no answer.)
    `the vessel`
        IS A STRING @desc The vessel, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 137
`punishment prescribed by s 137` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "137"
    words                    IS "fine not exceeding $1,500"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 137 of the Penal Code 1871 (deserter concealed on board a merchant vessel through the negligence of the master)
GIVEN f IS A `Deserter on Merchant Vessel Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 137` f IF
        "The"
    AND f's `the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel`
    AND f's `on board of which any deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore is concealed`
    AND "shall, though ignorant of such concealment, be punished ... if"
    AND f's `he might have known of such concealment, but for some neglect of his duty as such master or person in charge, or but for some want of discipline on board of the vessel`

@export Frame a charge under section 137 of the Penal Code 1871 (deserter concealed on board a merchant vessel through the negligence of the master), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Deserter on Merchant Vessel Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 137` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "137" "deserter concealed on board a merchant vessel through the negligence of the master"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 137`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 137` f)
        (CONCAT "being the master of ", f's `the vessel`, ", a merchant vessel on board of which a deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces was concealed, might have known of such concealment but for some neglect of your duty as such master or some want of discipline on board of the vessel", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel`) "the master or person in charge of a merchant vessel"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `on board of which any deserter from the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore is concealed`) "a deserter concealed on board"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `he might have known of such concealment, but for some neglect of his duty as such master or person in charge, or but for some want of discipline on board of the vessel`) "might have known of the concealment but for neglect of duty or want of discipline")))

§§ `s 138 - Abetment of act of insubordination by an officer or a serviceman`

--   138. Whoever abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by an
--   officer or any serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting
--   forces lawfully present in Singapore, shall, if such act of insubordination
--   be committed in consequence of that abetment, be punished with imprisonment
--   for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 138
`punishment prescribed by s 138` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "138"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 138 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an act of insubordination by an officer or serviceman)
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 138` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by such officer or serviceman`
    AND (    f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
         OR  f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it` )
    AND "shall, if"
    AND f's `such act of insubordination is committed in consequence of that abetment`

@export Frame a charge under section 138 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment of an act of insubordination by an officer or a serviceman), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Armed Forces Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 138` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "138" "abetment of an act of insubordination by an officer or a serviceman"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 138`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 138` f)
        (CONCAT "did abet what you knew to be an act of insubordination by ", `one person` (f's `the serviceman`), ", and such act of insubordination was committed in consequence of that abetment", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by such officer or serviceman`) "abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an officer or a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore` OR f's `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to it`) "by an officer or serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by section 140B, the Singapore Police Force)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `such act of insubordination is committed in consequence of that abetment`) "such act of insubordination is committed in consequence of that abetment")))

§§ `s 139 - Saving`

--   139. Where provision is made in any law relating to the discipline of the
--   Singapore Armed Forces for the punishment of an offence corresponding to an
--   offence defined in this Chapter, no person who is subject to such provision
--   shall be subject to punishment under this Code for the offence defined in
--   this Chapter.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 139
DECLARE `Service Discipline Saving Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `provision is made in any law relating to the discipline of the Singapore Armed Forces for the punishment of an offence corresponding to an offence defined in this Chapter`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law on Singapore Armed Forces discipline (for example the Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 - not in this job's inputs) provide for punishing an offence corresponding to the Chapter 7 offence in question?
    `the person is subject to such provision`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused subject to that provision?

-- A bar to punishment, not an element: like a general exception (PLAN section 5) it is
-- not repeated in the Chapter 7 ladders. At integration the charge sheet reads it
-- beside them. No charge of its own.
@export Whether section 139 of the Penal Code 1871 takes a person out of punishment under the Code for a Chapter 7 offence (service discipline saving)
GIVEN f IS A `Service Discipline Saving Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not subject to punishment under this Code within section 139` f IF
        "Where"
    AND f's `provision is made in any law relating to the discipline of the Singapore Armed Forces for the punishment of an offence corresponding to an offence defined in this Chapter`
    AND "no person who"
    AND f's `the person is subject to such provision`
    AND "shall be subject to punishment under this Code for the offence defined in this Chapter"

§§ `s 140 - Wearing the dress of a serviceman`

--   140. Whoever, not being a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any
--   visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore, wears any garb or carries any
--   token resembling any garb or token used by such a serviceman, with the
--   intention that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with
--   fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 140; s 140B
DECLARE `Serviceman Garb Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `not being a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused NOT a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or visiting forces (or, by s 140B, a member of the Singapore Police Force)?
    `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by such a serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused wear a garb, or carry a token, resembling one used by such a serviceman (or police officer)?
    `with the intention that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend it to be believed that they were such a serviceman?
    `the garb or token`
        IS A STRING @desc The garb or token, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 140
`punishment prescribed by s 140` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "140"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 140 of the Penal Code 1871 (wearing the dress of a serviceman)
GIVEN f IS A `Serviceman Garb Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 140` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    AND f's `not being a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`
    AND f's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by such a serviceman`
    AND f's `with the intention that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman`

@export Frame a charge under section 140 of the Penal Code 1871 (wearing the dress of a serviceman), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Serviceman Garb Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 140` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "140" "wearing the dress of a serviceman"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 140`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 140` f)
        (CONCAT "not being a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces, did wear or carry ", f's `the garb or token`, ", resembling a garb or token used by such a serviceman, with the intention that it might be believed that you were such a serviceman", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `not being a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces lawfully present in Singapore`) "not being a serviceman"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by such a serviceman`) "wears a garb or carries a token resembling one used by such a serviceman"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman`) "with the intention that it may be believed that he is such a serviceman")))

§§ `s 140A - "Harbour"`

--   140A. In this Chapter, "harbour" includes the supplying a person with
--   shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of
--   conveyance, or the assisting a person in any way to evade apprehension.

-- The same words as s 130A, for Chapter 7; the drill-down for s 136's harbouring leaf.
@export Whether the accused "harbours" a person, as Chapter 7 of the Penal Code 1871 uses the word (s 140A)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbour Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours within section 140A` f IF
        "In this Chapter, 'harbour' includes"
    ..  f's `harbours the person in the ordinary sense of the word`
    OR  f's `supplies the person with shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition, or means of conveyance`
    OR  f's `assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`

§§ `s 140B - Application of Chapter 7 to Singapore Police Force`

--   140B. The provisions of this Chapter relating to offences committed in
--   relation to members of the Singapore Armed Forces or any visiting forces
--   lawfully present in Singapore shall apply, with the necessary modifications,
--   to similar acts committed in relation to members of the Singapore Police
--   Force or any volunteer, auxiliary or special force attached to, or coming
--   under the jurisdiction of, that Force.

-- Encoded as the leaf `a member of the Singapore Police Force or any volunteer,
-- auxiliary or special force attached to it`, ORed with the armed-forces leaf in
-- every Chapter 7 ladder, and named in the @desc of ss 137 and 140's leaves.
